<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Crown Domain of the Nguyen Dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1950 CE – 1955 CE · capital Ban Me Thuot</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A special status zone of 1950 to 1955 placing Vietnam's Central Highlands and some upland areas under Bao Dai's personal authority.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In April 1950 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a>, head of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-vietnam">State of Vietnam</a>, decreed that the Central Highlands and other upland areas inhabited mainly by ethnic minorities would form the Hoang trieu Cuong tho, Crown Domain, directly under the Nguyen crown rather than the ordinary government. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nung-people">Nung</a> and Tai areas of the north were also attached.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The domain was administered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buon-ma-thuot">Ban Me Thuot</a> under a separate statute that protected highland peoples' land and customs, limited lowland Vietnamese settlement and kept French military and planter influence strong. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> used the highlands for hunting and as a personal power base, with residences at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-lat">Da Lat</a> and Ban Me Thuot.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-geneva">Geneva</a> Accords of 1954 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai's</a> deposition by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-dinh-diem">Ngo Dinh Diem</a> in 1955, the Crown Domain was abolished, and the highlands were integrated into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-vietnam">Republic of Vietnam</a>, opening them to large-scale Vietnamese settlement.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/crown-domain-of-the-nguyen-dynasty.jpg" alt="Crown Domain of the Nguyen Dynasty" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: (many, see history) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Vietnam.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1950 CE – 1955 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ban Me Thuot</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bao Dai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Animism, Buddhism, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese, Rhade, Jarai</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hoàng triều Cương thổ, Crown Domain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=crown-domain-of-the-nguyen-dynasty" aria-label="Crown Domain of the Nguyen Dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7508 1375 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Crown Domain of the Nguyen Dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7939 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7828 1631h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7828 1631h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Vietnam. <a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=crown-domain-of-the-nguyen-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

